:: Pub Gentlemans Club
    <<effects>><<set $xchange.landryGentlemansIntro to 1>>

    "The Gentleman's club?" Landry looks at you, puzzled. <<He>> leans back. "Yes, of course I know about them. They are a shadowy organisation dedicated to serving the non-con exhibitionism market." <<He>> takes out a bunch of coins from <<his>> pocket and begins laying them down on the table in a grid-like pattern on one side. Then, <<he>> places a picture of a random young-looking person on the other, and a "Gentleman's club"-engraved poker chip between them.
    <br><br>

    "Their operation mainly deals with sourcing exploitable individuals and linking them to paying customers who'll want to make them do stuff under duress," <<he>> moves the coins to the chip, and stacks them neatly. Before finally taking a few coins from the top and placing them on the photo. 
    <br><br>

    "They employ the carrot and the stick method, by both blackmailing <i>and rewarding</i> the victims, in order to keep them compliant and malleable during the early period in which they are still able to resist," <<he>> explains. "Once the victims are deep enough in trouble, they withhold any and all rewards, pocketing them as profit."
    <br><br>

    "Their business model is quite ingenious, if I do say so myself," <<he>> remarks.
    <br><br>

    <<link [[Look at the chip|Pub Gentlemans Club 2]]>><</link>>

:: Pub Gentlemans Club 2
    <<effects>>

    The poker chip is quite ornate. Precious gems of various kinds decorate the outer ring of the chip, while a luxurious gold coats every bit and every depression surrounding the ebony black core at the centre. A silvery engraving etched into the material, reading <i>"Gentleman's Club: Black Member"</i>.

    Landry catches you staring intently at the poker chip. "Oh, this? Yeah, I'm subscribed to the club myself," <<he>> confesses. "Can't blame me. Their material's top notch."
    <br><br>

    Your blood boils under your skin, as you struggle to express everything you hold within. Then, finally Landry realises. "Oh shit! Wait a minute," <<he>> jumps off <<his>> seat. But before <<he>> attracts too much attention to <<himself>>, <<he>> manages to restrain <<his>> voice. "Are you perhaps that hugely popular new entrant that's been making the rounds among the outer circles? No wonder you were asking about them."
    <br><br>

    <<He>> notices you shooting daggers with your eyes. "Oh, no no no!" <<he>> hurries to clarify. "I'm only in the club because there's an awkward little <<nnpc_gendery "Kylar">> who I always fancy looking at." Landry plays it off as nothing. "This <<nnpc_gendery "Kylar">>'s a bit of psycho, so we don't meddle in <<nnpc_his "Kylar">> affairs. Yet trouble always has a way of finding <<nnpc_him "Kylar">> and making things lewd."
    <br><br>

    It seems Landry might really go on and on endlessly about this "<<nnpc_gendery "Kylar">>". But you still have a problem to solve, so you cut <<him>> off.
    <br><br>

    <<link [[Ask about stopping the blackmail|Pub Gentlemans Club 3]]>><</link>>

:: Pub Gentlemans Club 3
    <<effects>>

    Landry scratches <<his>> chin, deep in thought for a few moments. "I guess I could convince a few influential members to hype up some other new blood," <<he>> suggests. "Which would in turn draw attention away from you."
    <br><br>

    Angry, you move to shoot down the plan, but <<he>> retorts. "Come on! That's the best I can do," Landry shows an apologetic look. "It's not like I can destroy that organisation. They are too powerful. Be reasonable." Still a bit hot-headed from the discovery of Landry's involvement with the club, you decide to take breath in before finally inquiring further.
    <br><br>

    "The plan would require <<printmoney 1500000>>," <<he>> explains. "So I can bribe those over which I hold no sway." You wince involuntarily at the price tag.
    <br><br>

    "Expensive, I know," <<he>> agrees. "But you must also understand that this won't be a permanent solution either." <<He>> exhales wearily as <<he>> leans forward to whisper. "Look. The club is full of powerful, capricious people," Landry pauses for a moment to think. "This will likely buy you <span class="blue">a month of peace</span> at the very least. Perhaps more, but only if you are careful."
    <br><br>

    <<if $money gte 1500000>>
        <<link [[Stop blackmail (£15000)|Pub Gentlemans Club Pay]]>>
            <<set $money -= 1500000>>
            <<set $xchange.blackmailHalt to 30>>
            <<blackmail-endquest>>
            <<set $xchange.blackmail.hasMaterial to false>>
            <<set $xchange.blackmail.hasNewMaterial to false>>
        <</link>>
    <<else>>
        You don't have enough cash.
    <</if>>
    <br>
    <<link [[Later|Pub Gentlemans Club Refuse]]>><</link>>
    <br>

:: Pub Gentlemans Club 4
    <<effects>>

    "Back again about the Gentleman's club?" Landry reclines. "It'll be <<printmoney 1500000>> to make them take their sights off from you for only a month." <<He>> looks disinterested on the surface. But you know this topic makes <<him>> nervous. 
    <br><br>

    Pulling the wool over powerful people's eyes is a big risk for anyone to take, so you can understand <<his>> legitimate concern.
    <br><br>

    <<if $money gte 1500000>>
        <<link [[Stop blackmail (£15000)|Pub Gentlemans Club Pay]]>>
            <<set $money -= 1500000>>
            <<set $xchange.blackmailHalt to 30>>
            <<blackmail-endquest>>
            <<set $xchange.blackmail.hasMaterial to false>>
            <<set $xchange.blackmail.hasNewMaterial to false>>
        <</link>>
    <<else>>
        You don't have enough cash.
    <</if>>
    <br>
    <<link [[Later|Pub Gentlemans Club Refuse]]>><</link>>
    <br>

:: Pub Gentlemans Club Pay
    <<effects>>

    "That's the spirit," Landry makes a show of counting the money. "If you had any tasks assigned to you, now it should be safe to disregard them. I'll take care of everything." <<He>> looks up for a moment, meeting your eyes. "But you better remember to lay low, or you'll sure as debt find yourself back again under their sights."
    <br><br>
    
    <<link [[Next|Pub Landry]]>><</link>>

:: Pub Gentlemans Club Refuse
    <<effects>>

    "Very well, then." Landry leans back into <<his>> chair. "As you prefer," <<he>> adds. "Let me know if you change your mind."
    <br><br>

    <<link [[Next|Pub Landry]]>><</link>>